      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, let me try to understand this. If we plan to improve the WARN/BUG behavior, I guess they will be similar to the linux kernel\u0027s usage? Then, WARN_ON/WARN_ON_ONCE will just print a warning log in the debug mode and then continue by skipping the warn instruction, so we are still in the infinite spin loop for the debug node. And for non-debug mode, WARN_ON/WARN_ON_ONCE will still do nothing? If so, it means we prefer to just print some warning log and continue the spin loop rather than hang the system, right?",
